      "writtenOn": "2025-02-14T00:23:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think it would be useful to beef up the tests a little bit, and also to make them more realistic. In particular, here you don\u0027t test at all for removing the blocking rule, nor do you test the arguments, so this test doesn\u0027t really help build much confidence that the correct addresses and ports are blocked and unblocked.\n\nSome things to consider doing :\n• Try with varied LinkProperties to make sure that the correct addresses, ports and protocols are indeed blocked\n• Connect, update the LP with some new addresses, make sure that the new subnet has the correct carveouts\n• Make sure that no other port has been allowed\n• Make sure that the allow rule is removed upon disconnection and upon removal of the IP address",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 123,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 123,
        "endChar": 5
      },
      "revId": "049d3b4f58d9bc33aecc9c68c93e92c07acc8501",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
